  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word often used in business, military, and project contexts. Emphasizes the completion aspect more strongly than {達成|たっせい}, which focuses on achievement.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {任務|にんむ}を{完遂|かんすい}する (to accomplish a mission)\n- {計画|けいかく}を{完遂|かんすい}する (to carry out a plan)\n- {目標|もくひょう}の{完遂|かんすい} (completion of a goal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {達成|たっせい}: achievement — focuses on reaching a goal, less emphasis on the process\n- {遂行|すいこう}: execution, carrying out — focuses on the process of performing a task",
